                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Laboratory diagnostics is a critical interdisciplinary field that bridges basic medical sciences and clinical practice. It is also an independent discipline that focuses on the fundamental theories and methodologies of disease diagnosis through laboratory testing.<br>Through the study and practical training in clinical laboratory diagnostics, students will gain an appreciation of the vital role that laboratory diagnostics play in clinical diagnosis and treatment. They will learn to accurately interpret laboratory results, deepen their understanding of various diagnostic tests, and improve their ability to apply this knowledge in clinical settings. The course also provides foundational support for scientific research, disease prevention, health education, genetic counseling, and related fields.<br>This semester’s Laboratory Diagnostics course is divided into five main sections:<br>1. &nbsp; &nbsp;Introduction to the Role of Laboratory Medicine and Specimen Collection<br>2. &nbsp; &nbsp;Overview of Common Laboratory Techniques<br>3. &nbsp; &nbsp;Blood Cell Analysis and Peripheral Blood Smear Examination<br>4. &nbsp; &nbsp;Bone Marrow Cytology, Urinalysis, and Fecal Examinations<br>5. &nbsp; &nbsp;Interpretation and Analysis of Laboratory Test Results</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
